```

`processMultiValue` (lines 355-367):
```java
for (int groupId : groupIds) {
    if (!_flags[groupId]) {        // line 360 — same unguarded index
        _numKeys++;
        _flags[groupId] = true;
    }
    ...
}
```

The iterator over group keys also walks up to `_globalGroupIdUpperBound` (lines 381-388). The class comment (line 65) documents the intended invariant: `globalGroupIdUpperBound is always smaller or equal to numGroupsLimit`, confirming `_flags` is sized by the limit while raw group ids come from the full cardinality product — the AIOOBE trigger when distinct keys exceed numGroupsLimit.

The map-based holders (`IntMapBasedHolder` lines ~630, `LongMapBasedHolder` ~659, `ArrayMapBasedHolder` ~839) instead use `getGroupId(...)` which returns `INVALID_ID` past the bound rather than indexing an array, so they are not affected."}

